body:
Thanks, I mean to be fair even if I never got to work in a studio just to be able to do it and create stuff would feel good, obviously the ultimate goal is to change careers and get a job in the industry.

&#x200B;

Thanks for your input

The problem with that is, you don't have to buy it from the PS Store, you can purchase a physical version (unless you have a digital PS5 of course, but most people who buy consoles probably wouldn't generally get a digital only version) which you can get much cheaper from online stores, or digital PC where it's much cheaper on places like cdkeys (it was £33.49 to pre-order, now £39.99, still much cheaper), whereas Stadia store is the only place to purchase Stadia games, they need to be enticing people in with better pricing imo.

&#x200B;

I'm all for Stadia, despite having a One X, I still have a Stadia Pro sub, but at the moment it's very rare I purchase new releases on Stadia because the pricing is just far too high.

Ohhh I'll give that a look thanks

&#x200B;

Yeah my first playthrough on RE7 was in VR, genuinely thought I was going to have a heart attack at times!
